{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf","id":1527273,"title":"[W5] Should the Cult of Fenris be the Cult of Wolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-22T15:25:44-08:00","id":1527273,"title":"[W5] Should the Cult of Fenris be the Cult of Wolf?","content":"They renamed multiple tribes to get rid of their cultural origins but the Cult of Fenris is still tied rather dramatically with a figure from Norse Mythology.<br /> <br /> Shouldn't they be the Cult of Wolf?<br /> <br /> It would make more sense and would still be fine as a name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T15:34:20-08:00","id":1527276,"title":"","content":"Honestly, you shouldn't tie the very spirit of the species the characters are (supposedly, if we are to believe the dog-hispo thing.)<br /> <br /> I'd actually say it could be something like the Cult of Wolverine or the Cult of Long Winter and work better. A spirit that, alongside the original cult, got fed up with the inaction of the Nation and took action on their own.<br /> <br /> That way, we'd also open the doors for the cult to be more than just a thin-veiled effort to make the Fenrir the worst of the lot. If the Cult was a multi-tribal group that included the most extreme members of each tribe, then suddenly you could still have Fenrir as PCs and use the Red Talon example characters in a much more fitting context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T16:18:18-08:00","id":1527279,"title":"","content":"One Tribe getting Wolf as a Patron is a horrible idea regardless of the status of the Cult. W5 is still full of cultural references even if they scrubbed off the most obvious things (The Black Furies still follow Gorgon... a Greek mythological type of being, for example). So a monster from a specific culture isn't actually out of bounds as things are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T19:30:30-08:00","id":1527282,"title":"","content":"I am not familiar with all the changes with the Get of Fenris so I am limiting my remarks on renaming Fenris as a more universal totem.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to use &quot;Wolf&quot; because that implies Fenris is the Father Wolf (totemic spirit of all Garou) as opposed to an aspect of Wolf like Winter Wolf or Old Wolf of the Woods.<br /> <br /> However, one could use something like the Fen Dwelling Wolf (which is what Fenris Wolf means) or the Apocalypse Wolf (for his role in the final battle) or the Bloody Wolf or similar (if you want to highlight his war aspects) or something else that is poetic for some role.<br /> <br /> I think Fenris is fine to keep as a name that is evocative and immediately explains what the spirit is like. But my take is that the Garou predate all the human cultures most identified with the homid side of the tribe so I am fine for having some other name that can be used as well as long as the earlier name isn't treated like it's been purged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T00:23:15-08:00","id":1527290,"title":"","content":"Aside from the Patron Spirit being Wolf, I think the other part is questionable too. Why call it a cult? I imagine that's where the idea for the torture brainwashing scene came from. Because it's called a cult and so that writer at Renegade Games thought of cult-like actions. But it's clear that then quickly enters BSD territory.<br /> <br /> Them being these Rage-fueled extremists also doesn't work. After all, it's not like you have the CoF on one side too much driven by Rage and the other Garou on the other hand being this faction that's very careful about how Rage affects them overly concerned with restraining themselves. And reading bits like the &quot;problem with Garou &quot; section, it's hard to see a distinction between Garou and the CoF. WtF did that much better in giving the Uratha and the Pure two distinctive ideologies. A sourcebook needs to get on this ASAP and give the CoF a similar treatment.<br /> <br /> CoF isn't supposed to be BSD-lite and they have to be more distinct from the other Garou. So I think in this case I think making the Patron Spirit Fenris, the Apocalypse Beast would work better and give them maybe a bit more of a Millenarian flavor in their ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T11:11:41-08:00","id":1527310,"title":"","content":"I query is the free Renegade material and the adventures supposed to be canon or 'variant-lore' as it ranges pretty far from what's established in the Core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T11:41:01-08:00","id":1527313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527310#post1527310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I query is the free Renegade material and the adventures supposed to be canon or 'variant-lore' as it ranges pretty far from what's established in the Core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're as canon as any module.<br /> <br /> Which is typically, &quot;All the background material is true but the events are non-determinate.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T11:56:12-08:00","id":1527316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527313#post1527313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they're as canon as any module.<br /> <br /> Which is typically, &quot;All the background material is true but the events are non-determinate.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But they kind of re-write a bunch of CoF material from the Core....though I guess it could all only apply to that small section of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T11:59:54-08:00","id":1527317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527316#post1527316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they kind of re-write a bunch of CoF material from the Core....though I guess it could all only apply to that small section of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh?<br /> <br /> I haven't read beyond W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T13:40:23-08:00","id":1527325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527317#post1527317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh?<br /> <br /> I haven't read beyond W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the adventure Deepest of Wounds. The bit that's talked about the most is the CoF using a torture brainwashing device called Maggot Symphony. But the setup is equally strange in how it differs from the corebook. For one, it establishes that Fenrir and other Garou work together. When the Fenrir leave for a raid (after their caern suddenly dries up), Garou from other Tribes join them. What is at issue is more that some Garou don't believe in the raiding party. And the adventure starts with the remnants of that raiding party coming back looking for new recruits and resources. Also, without the torture brainwashing stuff, there are Garou who would join the raiding party. Very different dynamics are at play in that adventure.<br /> <br /> Only time will tell if Renegade just has a different take or if this was a one off.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T06:17:27-08:00","id":1527370,"title":"","content":"Tangentially I think making their Patron Wolf would be a mistake, much like Fly and Bat, and I felt the same about previous animal ones that weren't called out as Banes taking those animal forms. Bat being an exception in that they were Gaian but fell into despair when the Camazotz were wiped out and only recently salvaged by the Shadow Lords, much like Lion almost fell when the White Howlers did.<br /> <br /> Whipoorwhill was clearly stated to be a Bane that embodied the Whipoorwhill call as an omen of death and not a spirit of the bird itself.<br /> <br /> Wolves still get a ton of bad press, making them the Patron of Purity obsessed Fascist expys just icks me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 12-24-2023, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T10:16:58-08:00","id":1527382,"title":"","content":"As I'll bring up in Phase Four of my W5 review, the Cult of Fenris was originally just a camp of an unnamed, unknown Tribe that the Cult wound up taking complete control of. Those that didn't join up became renunciates and joined up with new Tribes, for the most part as tribeless Garou don't exist it in W5 it seems. As such, the Tribe's Patron allowed it to happen and 'remains' the Patron, although there is speculation on whether or not it is the same spirit or if it has been tainted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T10:19:42-08:00","id":1527383,"title":"","content":"The only real problem with Whippoorwill, is that it doesn't make any sense. The only associations of whippoorwills to anything other than just being birds that are old enough to make sense as a Patron for the Black Spiral Dancers, are Native American in origin. The old editions never really explained why a North American bird became the spirit of a Garou Tribe associated with the Picts.<br /> <br /> Even in W5, it would still be weird to have such a localized animal as a spirit of that level of power/relation to the Garou. It would be like the Glass Walkers following Golden Orb Weaver instead of just Spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T14:42:26-08:00","id":1527396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527383#post1527383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only real problem with Whippoorwill, is that it doesn't make any sense. The only associations of whippoorwills to anything other than just being birds that are old enough to make sense as a Patron for the Black Spiral Dancers, are Native American in origin. The old editions never really explained why a North American bird became the spirit of a Garou Tribe associated with the Picts.<br /> <br /> Even in W5, it would still be weird to have such a localized animal as a spirit of that level of power/relation to the Garou. It would be like the Glass Walkers following Golden Orb Weaver instead of just Spider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured it was just the US ones that followed the Whipporwhill Bane and with the US Dancers having the most numbers it is the Tribal Patron by sheer inertia Green Dragon was certainly much more prevalent amongst European packs in the past for example. Kirijama dominates in northern Beast Courts territories etc. I think the BSDs are just too fractured by the individual Urge Wyrms to have a single Tribal Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T14:52:23-08:00","id":1527397,"title":"","content":"It's just a hypothesis, but they may have kept it because Fenrir connects with Ragnarok which would be an apocalypse so to speak, to show how far the situation has evolved for CoF or they really wanted to show that that was the W5 version of GoF to end keep people quiet about the controversies of this tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T20:16:23-08:00","id":1527407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527396#post1527396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I figured it was just the US ones that followed the Whipporwhill Bane and with the US Dancers having the most numbers it is the Tribal Patron by sheer inertia Green Dragon was certainly much more prevalent amongst European packs in the past for example. Kirijama dominates in northern Beast Courts territories etc. I think the BSDs are just too fractured by the individual Urge Wyrms to have a single Tribal Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would probably would have been better for either legacy or W5 to use your idea of the BSDs not having a single Tribal Totem after they grew in numbers vastly beyond the White Howlers.<br /> <br /> But as that wasn't the case, it doesn't really address why, in the supposed nature of spirit hierarchies, the BSDs would follow far more specific ones (and thus weaker ones) than broader ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T23:27:00-08:00","id":1527408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527407#post1527407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would probably would have been better for either legacy or W5 to use your idea of the BSDs not having a single Tribal Totem after they grew in numbers vastly beyond the White Howlers.<br /> <br /> But as that wasn't the case, it doesn't really address why, in the supposed nature of spirit hierarchies, the BSDs would follow far more specific ones (and thus weaker ones) than broader ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I didn't understand why tribal totems existed in the first place because there's implied to be countless totem types. It's not like the Wyrm is lacking for Incarnae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T23:55:14-08:00","id":1527409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527397#post1527397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just a hypothesis, but they may have kept it because Fenrir connects with Ragnarok which would be an apocalypse so to speak, to show how far the situation has evolved for CoF or they really wanted to show that that was the W5 version of GoF to end keep people quiet about the controversies of this tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint: W:tA often engages in turning myths on their heads so that humans look out of touch at minimum and often willfully self-destructive. See also, the Black Furies and how most of the heroes of Greek myth were in league with the Wyrm. Difficulty: Really only works for non-marginalized cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T03:41:14-08:00","id":1527415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527397#post1527397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just a hypothesis, but they may have kept it because Fenrir connects with Ragnarok which would be an apocalypse so to speak, to show how far the situation has evolved for CoF or they really wanted to show that that was the W5 version of GoF to end keep people quiet about the controversies of this tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the funny bit. In old Werewolf Fenris was not tied into Ragnarok. He was painted as such thanks to the cults of Wotan who they were fighting - Werewolves were Satan/Surtr to the followers of the Aesir and their dark Wolf God was the greatest terror of them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 12-25-2023, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T03:49:59-08:00","id":1527416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527396#post1527396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I figured it was just the US ones that followed the Whipporwhill Bane and with the US Dancers having the most numbers it is the Tribal Patron by sheer inertia Green Dragon was certainly much more prevalent amongst European packs in the past for example. Kirijama dominates in northern Beast Courts territories etc. I think the BSDs are just too fractured by the individual Urge Wyrms to have a single Tribal Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good way to treat it in practical terms, but usually one Totem is the supreme patron of the tribe with others being allies/servants. So it does create some issues here. I usually just don't delve into what the totem of the BSD is for that reason and the only time it came up in the game I used visions of the Black Spiral itself.<br /> <br /> Which does make me wonder - What if their totem would be that and its only servitors you could commune with in practical way would be the spirits dwelling within - like the dark reflection of the Whipporwill, the mad aspect of Bat, The Green Dragon and all others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T05:56:23-08:00","id":1527420,"title":"","content":"My solution for the BSD patron is this; They started with Shrike until they arrived to the Americas and there Whippoorwill became a much better one. Or that both were just aspects of a larger Evil Bird Incarna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T10:34:35-08:00","id":1527433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527409#post1527409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Counterpoint: W:tA often engages in turning myths on their heads so that humans look out of touch at minimum and often willfully self-destructive. See also, the Black Furies and how most of the heroes of Greek myth were in league with the Wyrm. Difficulty: Really only works for non-marginalized cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I think the Patriarch is still in horrible taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T12:42:09-08:00","id":1527436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527433#post1527433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I think the Patriarch is still in horrible taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Patriarch is an expression of organised religion being used to control society and shape Faith into Dogma. There is nothing in poor taste about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T13:15:53-08:00","id":1527437,"title":"","content":"As a further elaboration, the Patriarch is not guaranteed at all to be &quot;God&quot;, whatever that might be, but humans don't have good inroads with the spirit world or spiritual knowledge in W:tA, so they can be bilked into believing that any spirit is what they think it is, and lots of spirits know this and take ruthless advantage of it. This actually crops up a lot more in KotE, though; even some Hungry Dead took up disguising themselves as &quot;deities&quot; in order to reap the benefits of having a small but devoted cult, but those that try to co-opt more established followers of more widely-noted figures tended to disappear, with few willing to speak of how or why the end came.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T13:42:50-08:00","id":1527438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527436#post1527436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Patriarch is an expression of organised religion being used to control society and shape Faith into Dogma.</div> </div> </div> </div>As originally described in the first Black Furies tribebook, the Patriarch is simply the Incarna of &quot;Man&quot; jealous of &quot;Woman&quot; (presumably because men cannot give birth in some kind of metaphysical explanation, though the details on why an individual man hates a woman could be anything) and is a servant of the Urge Wyrm of Hate, Abhorra. So by itself, it actually has nothing to do with religion. It is just misogyny. Though religion could be a cover to justify male oppression of women, religion doesn't need to be involved. The Patriarch would work through whatever means available. An incel would be someone susceptible to the Patriarch even though religion has nothing to do with his hatred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527436#post1527436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing in poor taste about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't know what specifically CTPhipps meant by it, I assume it's because of later identification of the Patriarch with specifically the God of Abrahamic monotheism. But I can't remember if that was explicitly stated in any subsequent sourcebook. Maybe it's just a fan notion? That's fairly silly because plenty of non-monotheistic religions are heavily patriarchal (not to mention early Christianity was extremely attractive to a lot of women because of how much less patriarchal it was compared to the pagan religions of the Mediterranean and Middle East). The quote that leads the section on the Patriarch in the 1e tribebook is from a Hindu text so pretty far from Abrahamic monotheism. Plus as previously mentioned, the Patriarch actually isn't about religion. It's about misogyny in general.<br /> <br /> The Incarna could easily be called the Misogynist instead, and who knows perhaps that is what it is called by other tribes. There is probably also a Bane that fits the role of Misandrist though it is likely not as powerful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T13:51:51-08:00","id":1527439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527420#post1527420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My solution for the BSD patron is this; They started with Shrike until they arrived to the Americas and there Whippoorwill became a much better one. Or that both were just aspects of a larger Evil Bird Incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just use Nightjar as a substitute. Nightjars and whippoorwills are part of the same Family of birds (caprimulgidae), and the European nightjar has similar habits and sinister connotations as the whippoorwill does in North America. In the W20 corebook, the opening comic even mentions the Nightjar instead so people have since realized some things.<br /> <br /> The original authors clearly didn't realize that the whippoorwill was not in Europe and therefore was a bad choice for a tribe of corrupt werewolves in Scotland. But simply make it Nightjar and everything is easily explained including why BSDs in North America might refer to Nightjar as Whippoorwill. In the end, it's all just &quot;sinister bird that harms others supernaturally&quot;.<br /> <br /> Whether Nightjar/Whippoorwill is a corrupted Gaian spirit, or some kind of Bane who assumes its form is somewhat immaterial. Though individual STs will have their own preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T14:02:38-08:00","id":1527440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527438#post1527438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As originally described in the first Black Furies tribebook, the Patriarch is simply the Incarna of &quot;Man&quot; jealous of &quot;Woman&quot; (presumably because men cannot give birth in some kind of metaphysical explanation, though the details on why an individual man hates a woman could be anything) and is a servant of the Urge Wyrm of Hate, Abhorra. So by itself, it actually has nothing to do with religion. It is just misogyny. Though religion could be a cover to justify male oppression of women, religion doesn't need to be involved. The Patriarch would work through whatever means available. An incel would be someone susceptible to the Patriarch even though religion has nothing to do with his hatred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh <i>that</i> one. I thought he meant Patriarch, the Weaver Incarna from <b>Book of the Weaver</b> and incarnation of Dogma that some folks occasionally conflate with the Abrahamic god. that one didn't really appear all that much in the later books, but considering their descriptions I always assumed that one was the Spirit of Dogma and belonged to the Weaver while the other was the spirit of Toxic Masculinity and belonged to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527438#post1527438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't know what specifically CTPhipps meant by it, I assume it's because of later identification of the Patriarch with specifically the God of Abrahamic monotheism. But I can't remember if that was explicitly stated in any subsequent sourcebook. Maybe it's just a fan notion? That's fairly silly because plenty of non-monotheistic religions are heavily patriarchal (not to mention early Christianity was extremely attractive to a lot of women because of how much less patriarchal it was compared to the pagan religions of the Mediterranean and Middle East). The quote that leads the section on the Patriarch in the 1e tribebook is from a Hindu text so pretty far from Abrahamic monotheism. Plus as previously mentioned, the Patriarch actually isn't about religion. It's about misogyny in general.<br /> <br /> The Incarna could easily be called the Misogynist instead, and who knows perhaps that is what it is called by other tribes. There is probably also a Bane that fits the role of Misandrist though it is likely not as powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the combination of the Incarna and the monotheistic God is a common interpretation of the Patriarch from the Book of the Weaver, but it's not supported by the text itself. It speaks of Dogma and institutions. The Patriarch of 1st edition Black Furies got mostly ignored in the future books, and when Revised Tribebook Black Furies comes around to mentioning the (BF) Patriarch it presents it in less negative tones than the original ones. It presents it as opposition to the feminine that should be put into balance. It also notes that it's most likely a separate spirit from any Abrahamic God, even if some might conflate it.<br /> <br /> So at this point we technically have <b>three</b> Patriarchs:<ul><li>The Wyrmish Patriarch, the wicked spirit of toxic manhood (BF 1st Edition)</li> <li>The Weaver Patriarch, the Incarna of Dogma and organised religion (Book of the Weaver)</li> <li>The Neutral Patriarch, pair to the sacred feminine that is out of balance (BF Revised)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T14:21:24-08:00","id":1527441,"title":"","content":"Book of the Weaver mentions that its Patriarch is close to the Wyrm, in that &quot;corruption is on his breath&quot;. This is pretty much par for course for a number of Weaver spirits, because the Defiler is really good at riding down the webs and ruining them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T15:33:12-08:00","id":1527442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527441#post1527441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of the Weaver mentions that its Patriarch is close to the Wyrm, in that &quot;corruption is on his breath&quot;. This is pretty much par for course for a number of Weaver spirits, because the Defiler is really good at riding down the webs and ruining them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always read that as how church organisations are coopted and abused by negative actors, even if the proper morals most religions are about would be contrary to this. The one in the original TBBF was all about evil of the wicked patriarchy and less about evils of organised religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T19:28:38-08:00","id":1527446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527440#post1527440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So at this point we technically have <b>three</b> Patriarchs</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the strong suspicion they were all meant to be the same Incarna, but the individual writers relied on memory instead of reviewing the primary documents. I find various bits of lore in different editions or sourcebooks that contradict each other. And while sometimes the writer does intend it to be a retcon, more often it just appears to be a mistake - likely because someone relied on memory rather than hunting down the source material.<br /> <br /> I totally forgot about the Patriarch mentioned in the Book of the Weaver.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T21:01:50-08:00","id":1527450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527436#post1527436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Patriarch is an expression of organised religion being used to control society and shape Faith into Dogma. There is nothing in poor taste about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That all Abrahamic faiths is in service of the cause of absolute evil and fundamentally misogynist.<br /> <br /> Which hey, you may believe, but is still pretty awful.<br /> <br /> And I think they rolled back what was pretty clearly meant to be, &quot;Male dominated religion replacing female dominated religion&quot; in the Black Furies book and I think they made the Patriarch into a Weaver spirit in the Book of the Weaver because they wanted to soften the presentation of the Incarnae from being a straight Wyrm spirit.<br /> <br /> But hey, my Garou lore has a history of being erroneous due to my preconceived V:TM biases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-26-2023, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T22:41:07-08:00","id":1527453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527450#post1527450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That all Abrahamic faiths is in service of the cause of absolute evil and fundamentally misogynist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by nature. The Weaver sought to calcify Dogma, and the Wyrm, as noted several times before, is really, really good at twisting the Weaver's webs while trapped within them. You know how the WoD is supposed to be &quot;the real world, but darker?&quot; That means that something was watching everything terrible done in the service of religion, feeding off of it, and encouraging more of the worst parts to flourish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which hey, you may believe, but is still pretty awful.<br /> <br /> And I think they rolled back what was pretty clearly meant to be, &quot;Male dominated religion replacing female dominated religion&quot; in the Black Furies book and I think they made the Patriarch into a Weaver spirit in the Book of the Weaver because they wanted to soften the presentation of the Incarnae from being a straight Wyrm spirit. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't exactly say that they softened it. Maybe if you're going by the directness of the OG BFTB, it might seem that way, but per the final paragraph describing the Dogma seed,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book of the Weaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a horrible thought that one of humanity's highest virtues - faith - has been terribly mauled and all but destroyed by dogma gone insane. But in the World of Darkness, it seems that except for a minority of people, this is largely true.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the Patriarch isn't &quot;God&quot;, but rather a ruthless Weaver spirit stained with the blood of everyone that he's driven humanity to kill in the name of Dogma and teetering toward another corner of the Triat. Basically, a corrupter of faith, not the figure that the faith recognizes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But hey, my Garou lore has a history of being erroneous due to my preconceived V:TM biases. </div> </div> </div>Should we also bring up the whack interpretation of religion that is Demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T02:50:35-08:00","id":1527456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527453#post1527453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Patriarch isn't &quot;God&quot;, but rather a ruthless Weaver spirit stained with the blood of everyone that he's driven humanity to kill in the name of Dogma and teetering toward another corner of the Triat. Basically, a corrupter of faith, not the figure that the faith recognizes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And note that Patriarch isn't &quot;only&quot; about the Abrahamic religions. There are also other religions out there that are deeply dogmatic and mysoginistic. Just look at parts of India and elsewhere in Asia where women are deemed as &quot;unclean&quot; during their menstrual cycle, or what women are subjected to due to religious beliefs in parts of Africa. Patriarch represents those people and those beliefs just as much as any you might find in the Abrahamic religions. Any religion that oppresses women due to religious dogma falls, to some degree, under the influence of Patriarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T09:11:25-08:00","id":1527462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527450#post1527450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That all Abrahamic faiths is in service of the cause of absolute evil and fundamentally misogynist.<br /> <br /> Which hey, you may believe, but is still pretty awful.<br /> <br /> And I think they rolled back what was pretty clearly meant to be, &quot;Male dominated religion replacing female dominated religion&quot; in the Black Furies book and I think they made the Patriarch into a Weaver spirit in the Book of the Weaver because they wanted to soften the presentation of the Incarnae from being a straight Wyrm spirit.<br /> <br /> But hey, my Garou lore has a history of being erroneous due to my preconceived V:TM biases.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something that's often said in conversations online,but it's not what's said in the books. The Patriarch &lt;&gt; Abrahamic God. As you can see in the rest of the discussion we've identified three patriarchs<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527440#post1527440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So at this point we technically have <b>three</b> Patriarchs:<ul><li>The Wyrmish Patriarch, the wicked spirit of toxic manhood (BF 1st Edition)</li> <li>The Weaver Patriarch, the Incarna of Dogma and organised religion (Book of the Weaver)</li> <li>The Neutral Patriarch, pair to the sacred feminine that is out of balance (BF Revised)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I've had to go back to verify what is said in the First Edition book as I don't have that one in print and I had to see the exact context it's presented in. For the Second and the Third Patriarch we can safely say that the books don't claim they are the Abrahamic God for better or for worse. This one I had to dig up as I've only ever thumbed through it at a friend's place and mostly remember the awesome Spencer pieces.<br /> <br /> I'll preface the following with a general disdain for what the 1st Edition Tribebooks have to say on the tribes or the World, and that I find it deeply weird that Brucatto was the one to write a book about women's perspective on the World. This is a book from 1994 and this bleeds through each and every of its pores.<br /> <br /> On a read of the First Edtion TB Black Furies it speaks of the Patriarch's rise in the earliest days of mankind from man's jealousy of woman and stoking their deepest darkest desires to pillage both the woman and the world. This entity does not have a name during this period, but it exists way before the time Abrahamic faiths would rise - it speaks of times before the Impergium. This origin also has a weird quirk that it doesn't really explain the other Tribes or the idea of non-female Werewolves and places the Creation of the Furies above all other Tribes. Something Brucatto loved to do for any of the protagonists of his Werewolf books.<br /> <br /> The name of the Patriarch appears for the first time on the a page later &quot;rising in the Middle East&quot; and &quot;putting women in their place&quot;. This is the first part where it seems to tie into Abrahamic Faiths by claiming that &quot;Patriarch's prophets spoke of kindness and good intentions, they crushed Woman beneath laws of ownership and myths of Sin&quot;. It speaks of how the Feminine tempered the hatred of the Patriarch's cults through introducing love and forgiveness and the image of the Holy Mother. It does place the Crusades as battles between the Patriarchs Cults. It follows this up by claiming that the Pure Lands were clean of the Patriarch's taint, however the people placed Man over Woman, they use this as a justification for the war against the Pure Tribes (!?!?). What follows is a downright bizarre version of history about them keeping the Patriarch away from the Pure Lands (uhm, who were the first settlers of North America, again?) and how their influence led to such things as women's rights and women's vote in America. The Old Country Furies dislike the American furies and enc their successes.<br /> <br /> The Patriarch appears just once more before the end of this history of the Furies, and tellingly points suddenly into a different direction where they claim as his deeds &quot;bride-pyres in India&quot;, suddenly leaving the context of Abrahamic Faiths. It will be mentioned again in the context of the Third World where it paints South America, Middle East and Inda with the same brush.<br /> <br /> I got nothing, you are right. At one point in the history of Werewolf (the game) the Black Furies equated Abrahamic God with A Wyrmish Incarna of pure Hatred. The only thing I can say about this is that this is the same period where the coquettry between fascist ideals and recruiting young skinheads was seen as a source of strength for the Get of Fenris. We've gone long past that, and a lot of this text sounds like the edgy writings of someone who seeks to protest the evils of religion without questioning the further context and what this would mean in practical terms. We've got the inkling of the later context that it's not just Abrahamic Faiths that are to blame here, but a broader pattern, alas the author chooses to pay it only lip service in his rage at Christianity/Islam.<br /> <br /> I feel playing up the fact that there can be vastly powerful spirits that are feeding off bad patterns in human behaviour, including religion is the way to go. However, religion as a whole is not a bad thing. For many it gives purpose and succor and very few religions actually have tenets that would lead us to being horrible to each other. The Wyrm feeds on us being horrible to each other, and assuming the worst of someone just because he believes something we do not is the quickest road to its tender attentions<br /> <br /> <br /> And because reading 1st edition WW books makes me want to use song quotes, I'll end on this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream Theater</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would wish this on our people?<br /> And proclaim That His will be done<br /> Scriptures they heed have misled them\u200b<br /> All praise their sacrificed sons</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T09:23:26-08:00","id":1527502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527409#post1527409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Counterpoint: W:tA often engages in turning myths on their heads so that humans look out of touch at minimum and often willfully self-destructive. See also, the Black Furies and how most of the heroes of Greek myth were in league with the Wyrm. Difficulty: Really only works for non-marginalized cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether this is valid or not depends on the team that made the W5 and how much they care about it. I'm not sure how interested they are in knowing about the previous editions, especially doing a Rebbot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T11:29:22-08:00","id":1527507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527502#post1527502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether this is valid or not depends on the team that made the W5 and how much they care about it. I'm not sure how interested they are in knowing about the previous editions, especially doing a Rebbot.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Sambrano notes, we get that they are very familiar with some elements of the setting but oftentimes feel like they need to burn the house to rebuild it.<br /> <br /> Besides, that's not always a bad thing.<br /> <br /> No one wants THE SOUND OF FREEDOM tie-in group, The Seventh Generation, to make their return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T13:17:45-08:00","id":1527513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527507#post1527507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the Sambrano notes, we get that they are very familiar with some elements of the setting but oftentimes feel like they need to burn the house to rebuild it.<br /> <br /> Besides, that's not always a bad thing.<br /> <br /> No one wants THE SOUND OF FREEDOM tie-in group, The Seventh Generation, to make their return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I think for the sake of continuation, for example, reimagining the Fenrir in a way that keeps them as a playable faction is better rather than doing a meta-critique of the past by making them unplayable. And similarly any approach that feels like taking a concept and burning it down should be avoided as much as possible. That's the constraint you get with making WOD5E.<br /> <br /> Because if that constraint is ignored, why even bother with a fifth edition? Just make something CofD like that is inspired by WOD instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T13:54:15-08:00","id":1527516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527513#post1527513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I think for the sake of continuation, for example, reimagining the Fenrir in a way that keeps them as a playable faction is better rather than doing a meta-critique of the past by making them unplayable. And similarly any approach that feels like taking a concept and burning it down should be avoided as much as possible. That's the constraint you get with making WOD5E.<br /> <br /> Because if that constraint is ignored, why even bother with a fifth edition? Just make something CofD like that is inspired by WOD instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember the previous owners to Paradox, the EVE ONLINE people, that said that Old World of Darkness being the basis for the MMORPG got a standing ovation. They know where the money is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T15:24:00-08:00","id":1527519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527507#post1527507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the Sambrano notes, we get that they are very familiar with some elements of the setting but oftentimes feel like they need to burn the house to rebuild it.<br /> <br /> Besides, that's not always a bad thing.<br /> <br /> No one wants THE SOUND OF FREEDOM tie-in group, The Seventh Generation, to make their return.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, much like the Swords, as far as Revised-era lore is concerned, they're dead. They died. Albrecht lead the charge in killing them all, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T15:56:31-08:00","id":1527522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527519#post1527519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, much like the Swords, as far as Revised-era lore is concerned, they're dead. They died. Albrecht lead the charge in killing them all, even.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even if they were not... They were literally there to be murdered by the PC's. This was not a playable group and it was pegged as villians that need to be murdered ASAP. I mean, what are we shocked that people do horrible things to children? At least in Werewolf we get to do something cathartic about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T18:11:50-08:00","id":1527527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527519#post1527519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, much like the Swords, as far as Revised-era lore is concerned, they're dead. They died. Albrecht lead the charge in killing them all, even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but they got brought back by W20.<br /> <br /> Which may be why there was 