 of the early teens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T18:45:23-08:00","id":1527532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527527#post1527527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but they got brought back by W20.<br /> <br /> Which may be why there was confusion.<br /> <br /> I think that was because W20 rolled back the in-universe clock, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't really bring them back. They were forced to write a metaplot-neutral stance from early 1e. We covered this, I believe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oddly, I always felt that demon was very clever of the writers.<br /> <br /> Because it's very much a game about playing ANGELS.<br /> <br /> Beings who love humanity and want to cultivate their faith as well as adoration.<br /> <br /> However, that wouldn't have flown with the edgier audience of the early teens. </div> </div> </div>And all non-Abrahamic religions are just schemes by the Earthbound to reap Faith! Lucifer supports Christianity and Atheism to deny them worship!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T19:16:11-08:00","id":1527533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527527#post1527527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that was because W20 rolled back the in-universe clock, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But No. But Yes. Some things got rolled back, others got kept others got changed yet again. It's not like there is a clear cutoff there. Some of the W20 supplements treat very late Revised developments as facts while ignoring things that happened in 1st or 2nd edition.Choosing the bring back the Swords was a concious choice here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527528#post1527528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like they probably offed them because of:<br /> <br /> 1. The poor taste in general<br /> 2. The fact that they do uncomfortably resemble the conspiracy theories of the Far Right rather than the punkish progressive left that WW was supposed to be form the perspective of</div> </div> </div> </div>The 7th Generation got ganked about '96-'97. So 23-24 years before some Americans started making bizarre conspiracy theories about mysteries of the pizza boxes. WoD has always delved into urban legends and conspiracy theories as fodder for the strangeness of the world. It's not like our world doesn't have exploitation of children and people who would peddle them to the rich and famous as a factual problem (Epstein for instance), and considering how such suffering is nectar to the Wyrm it's bound to be worse in the WoD.<br /> <br /> I'd say that there are few things as punk as hunting down the rich and untouchable that can get away with exploiting the systems that should protect all of us.<br /> <br /> And their legacy lives on in the Apocalyptic Record, with a veteran of that conflict still trying to do damage control from the horrors they have done and fighting their remnants and/or successors.<br /> <br /> And if that's a bridge too far for you, I would like to remind you that quite a few vampires don't mind preying on the unprotected, to the point that some would feed only on them. That's of course before we walk into all the unfortunate rape, slavery and addiction that the Vampiric society fosters on its participants or victims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527529#post1527529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly, I always felt that demon was very clever of the writers.<br /> <br /> Because it's very much a game about playing ANGELS.<br /> <br /> Beings who love humanity and want to cultivate their faith as well as adoration.<br /> <br /> However, that wouldn't have flown with the edgier audience of the early teens.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more than edgy enough. All religion is a hoax created by demons bound in the Earth seeping into Humanity and getting them to project their power onto the world. Christianity specifically is Lucifer's secret weapon that he has made to fight all other religions and contain the Earthbound. How is this any better than Religion being a tool of cosmic evil? And it was written 8 years later, when they should have known better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 12-27-2023, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T20:09:20-08:00","id":1527534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527532#post1527532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all non-Abrahamic religions are just schemes by the Earthbound to reap Faith! Lucifer supports Christianity and Atheism to deny them worship!</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that argument doesn't really go over when Werewolf is canonically still true. It just muddied the waters when previously Abrahamic religions was just objectively wrong due to Mage and Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Mind you, there's also the fact that God is explicitly evil in Demon: The Fallen so there's another layer to the confusion.<br /> <br /> It's about as Pro-Abrahamic as the latter seasons of Supernatural.<br /> <br /> But then again, a lot of fans assume that each line are their own separate universe with lesser versions of the other splats versus a World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-27-2023, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T01:49:59-08:00","id":1527541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527528#post1527528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The fact that they do uncomfortably resemble the conspiracy theories of the Far Right rather than the punkish progressive left that WW was supposed to be form the perspective of</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't really speak highly of the decision makers, because it just implies a highly surface level understanding of what the Seventh Generation was involved with.<br /> <br /> 1) The Seventh Generation was very much about shining a light on the residential school programs used to commit cultural genocide of Native Americans and Indigenous peoples in Canada and the US. It's not about evil non-white people running child sex slave islands like said right wing conspiracy theory movie is about. It's also about things like the school to prison pipeline (though that's a more recent name than the older books would have known to get into). Yes, the Wyrm-cult of child sex criminal side gets very close to right-wing conspiracy theories, but it diverges hard into something very progressive: intersectionality, systemic institutional biases, and general traumas.<br /> <br /> One of the things the right-wing conspiracy theories always start to show their delusions around is when they get to motive. Why are is the secret cabal of elites doing all of these horrible things to children? They'll spill lots of digital ink on fantastical hypotheses, but they never add up. They're obviously wild guesses attempting to post-hoc justify that anything flies when it's the (liberal) global elites.<br /> <br /> The motives of the Seventh Generation are direct and about telling a pretty important allegory: they're an evil cult that does horrible things to children to make the world a worse place. They want to create a world where no child is safe from external trauma and abuse, so no child can grow up to be a healthy well adjusted person that might push back against the Wyrm's push to destroy the world. While they are over-the-top in WtA 2e fashion so they're also just evil shits to slaughter for being evil, they are exploiting things normal humans are already doing and making them worse (you know, like making it a setting that's darker than our world... a World of Darkness so to speak). The Seventh Generation is taking the way real world systemic issues destroy minority children's futures, and turn mainstream norms into toxic radicalization, and turning it up to 11. That's pretty progressive and pretty punk.<br /> <br /> 2) Sex trafficking and rich pieces of shit abusing children are real world ills regardless of right-wing nutjob conspiracy theories. Inane conspiracy theories are no reason to stop the real need to combat these tragedies; including using fiction to get people to realize that these problems are things to think about. If you want to argue that WtA isn't the game to address it, OK, though the Residential School system is plenty reason back when indigenous issues mattered to the game. Progressives can't stop fighting the MeToo fights (like, this year the Venice Film Festival defended having Roman Polanski, Woody Allen, and Luc Besson all having screenings despite their histories), Jefferey Epstein and the systems that let him operate for so long, the right-wing attempt to dismantle US public education and stop higher education when it goes places they don't like, and so on, just because there might be some overlap with conspiracy theories.<br /> <br /> It's not very punk to give up because bad people are overlapping what you do. Real punks rockers don't give up on punk because there are Nazis that perform punk-style music. They go on stage and tell Nazi &quot;punks&quot; to fuck off. Some of the biggest critics of The Sound of Freedom are people who actually deal with the reality of that bit of violent fantasy, because of hos misleading it is about what the real problems are, and how the real people fighting to fix them aren't action movie heroes; and rather they're hard working people regularly demonized by the people that love that film so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T02:29:07-08:00","id":1527543,"title":"","content":"Did I accidentally open a Pandora's box?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T10:57:14-08:00","id":1527560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527543#post1527543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I accidentally open a Pandora's box?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually appreciate this is one of the rare forums we can discuss the politics and subtext of the books without anyone taking it personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T16:44:39-08:00","id":1527581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527273-w5-should-the-cult-of-fenris-be-the-cult-of-wolf?p=1527541#post1527541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This doesn't really speak highly of the decision makers, because it just implies a highly surface level understanding of what the Seventh Generation was involved with.<br /> <br /> 1) The Seventh Generation was very much about shining a light on the residential school programs used to commit cultural genocide of Native Americans and Indigenous peoples in Canada and the US. It's not about evil non-white people running child sex slave islands like said right wing conspiracy theory movie is about. It's also about things like the school to prison pipeline (though that's a more recent name than the older books would have known to get into). Yes, the Wyrm-cult of child sex criminal side gets very close to right-wing conspiracy theories, but it diverges hard into something very progressive: intersectionality, systemic institutional biases, and general traumas.<br /> <br /> One of the things the right-wing conspiracy theories always start to show their delusions around is when they get to motive. Why are is the secret cabal of elites doing all of these horrible things to children? They'll spill lots of digital ink on fantastical hypotheses, but they never add up. They're obviously wild guesses attempting to post-hoc justify that anything flies when it's the (liberal) global elites.<br /> <br /> The motives of the Seventh Generation are direct and about telling a pretty important allegory: they're an evil cult that does horrible things to children to make the world a worse place. They want to create a world where no child is safe from external trauma and abuse, so no child can grow up to be a healthy well adjusted person that might push back against the Wyrm's push to destroy the world. While they are over-the-top in WtA 2e fashion so they're also just evil shits to slaughter for being evil, they are exploiting things normal humans are already doing and making them worse (you know, like making it a setting that's darker than our world... a World of Darkness so to speak). The Seventh Generation is taking the way real world systemic issues destroy minority children's futures, and turn mainstream norms into toxic radicalization, and turning it up to 11. That's pretty progressive and pretty punk.<br /> <br /> 2) Sex trafficking and rich pieces of shit abusing children are real world ills regardless of right-wing nutjob conspiracy theories. Inane conspiracy theories are no reason to stop the real need to combat these tragedies; including using fiction to get people to realize that these problems are things to think about. If you want to argue that WtA isn't the game to address it, OK, though the Residential School system is plenty reason back when indigenous issues mattered to the game. Progressives can't stop fighting the MeToo fights (like, this year the Venice Film Festival defended having Roman Polanski, Woody Allen, and Luc Besson all having screenings despite their histories), Jefferey Epstein and the systems that let him operate for so long, the right-wing attempt to dismantle US public education and stop higher education when it goes places they don't like, and so on, just because there might be some overlap with conspiracy theories.<br /> <br /> It's not very punk to give up because bad people are overlapping what you do. Real punks rockers don't give up on punk because there are Nazis that perform punk-style music. They go on stage and tell Nazi &quot;punks&quot; to fuck off. Some of the biggest critics of The Sound of Freedom are people who actually deal with the reality of that bit of violent fantasy, because of hos misleading it is about what the real problems are, and how the real people fighting to fix them aren't action movie heroes; and rather they're hard working people regularly demonized by the people that love that film so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compare to how W5 dealt with the issue of residential schools, which was to drop a Wikipedia-level description of them in the middle of their book with zero context or connection to the game and pat themselves on the back for addressing Important Issue while erasing Indigenous issues or representation everywhere else.<br /> <br /> It's something I sorely miss about games like pre-5th WtA and some other WoD games. Even if they were clumsy or offensive sometimes, they at least took a hard stand on things. The passion was clearly there. Many games these days are so terrified about the &quot;&quot;&quot;wrong people&quot;&quot;&quot; playing their games that other than some surface-level platitudes they refuse to say anything of substance at all. I would really love to see modern social awareness combined with that old passion, but at this rate I don't know if we'll ever truly get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}